>    Yeah, this is nice improvement, but not that fundamental. Instead
> of eating one corpse, you need to eat many of them until you get into
> a comfortable range. In the end, the situation is very similar, you
> just need to eat much more corpses. Sure, this would probably make you
> skip non-essential resistances etc.

You're thinking of SporkHack's resistances.

I haven't programmed and playtested anything yet (so this might
change) but I intend to have 4 of resistance level: none, little, much
and immune.

One resistance source should give you "little" and an intrinsic and
extrinsic source will give you "much".

You are only "immune" if you have the resistance by polymorph or by
role. E.g. barbarians would be immune to poison from the start.

This of course will also need changes to specific attacks otherwise
the instadeath rate in Gehennom would skyrocket.

